 ## Overview
-A Voxel Collision Test determines if a solid voxel exists within a specific spatial region, typically a vertical column defined by world XZ coordinates and a Y-axis slab range. It solves the problem of detecting physical obstructions in voxel-based environments, enabling mechanics such as walking through carved-out holes or detecting ground contact for entity physics. It differs from the parent [Voxel Occupancy Test](1281-voxel-occupancy-test.md), which tests individual points, by aggregating occupancy over a continuous volume (a column or slab) to return a single binary result for the region.
+A Voxel Collision Test determines if a solid voxel exists within a specific spatial region, typically a vertical column defined by world XZ coordinates and a Y-axis slab range [S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of detecting physical obstructions in voxel-based environments, enabling mechanics such as walking through carved-out holes or detecting ground contact for entity physics [S2, unofficial][S4, unofficial]. It differs from the parent [Voxel Occupancy Test](1281-voxel-occupancy-test.md), which tests individual points, by aggregating occupancy over a continuous volume (a column or slab) to return a single binary result for the region.
 
